{#
Generated by: Claude Code CLI
Date time: 2026/09/09 05:00 SAST
Version: 0.7
Description:
  The catalogue's category browser.

  Every branch that holds a course, nested, each accordion carrying the courses filed directly in it
  and its sub-categories as accordions inside it. A category holding nothing anywhere beneath it is
  not here at all: only a course makes a branch worth opening, and an empty one is a promise the
  page cannot keep.

  A parent holds its own courses and its children separately rather than pooling them, because
  pooling would list a course twice - once under the child it belongs to and once under the parent.
  The heading therefore reports two numbers where they differ: what this category holds, and what
  its whole branch holds.

  Each category pages its own courses. The tree is small - three levels of taxonomy - but a branch
  is not, so the bound belongs on the courses rather than on the categories. The `open` parameter
  names which accordion the page number belongs to, so paging one cannot move another, and every
  link is an ordinary GET that works with no JavaScript.

Changelog:
  2026/09/09 05:00 SAST
  - Created.
#}
{% extends layout %}

{% block page_body %}
	{% set ph_back_href = '/courses' %}
	{% set ph_back_label = 'Course catalogue' %}
	{% set ph_kicker = 'Browse' %}
	{% set ph_title = 'Browse by category' %}
	{% set ph_lead = 'Every part of the catalogue that holds a course. Open a category to see what is in it.' %}
	{% set ph_action_href = '/courses/tags' %}
	{% set ph_action_label = 'Browse by tag' %}
	{% include '@platform/partials/page-head.html.twig' %}

	<section class="container-fluid cl-container-wide py-5">
		{% if category_tree %}
			<div class="cl-category-tree">
				{% for node in category_tree %}
					{% include '@platform/partials/category-branch.html.twig' with {node: node, depth: 0} %}
				{% endfor %}
			</div>
		{% else %}
			<div class="empty section">
				<h3>No category holds a published course yet</h3>
				<p class="mb-0">A category appears here as soon as a published course is filed in it or in one of its sub-categories.</p>
			</div>
		{% endif %}
	</section>
{% endblock %}
